The .meta file allows you to add authors, ratings, and links.

The first line is used for the author, and you can add 'author:' before your name without it showing up in the author section./NOBR
If you instead write 'authors:' it will display 'Authors: {meta_authors}' instead of 'Author: {meta_author}'.

The second line is rating. Place 'rating: {rating}' here./NOBR
Ratings are: g, t, e, a./NOBR
G = General Audiences, T = Teen, E = Explicit, A = Adult

The third line is for links to your pages. Add 'links: {your links}' here.

The fourth line is for warnings. Add 'warnings: {your warnings}' here.

A fully-filled-out .meta file would look like this:

author: benheroblaw/NOBR/CONT
rating: t/NOBR/CONT
links: https://benheroblaw.github.io/NOBR/CONT
warnings: swearing/NOBR/CONT